WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.560 --> 00:00:02.869 align:start position:0%
 
working on television can be a great  experience but some actors end up with  serious misgivings about particular  shows on which they appeared  from teen stars to legendary comedians  there are a whole lot of actors who  seriously regret playing in certain tv  shows  when misha barton took on a lead role on  the teen soap the oc  she was already a star in the making the  show chronicled the lifestyles of the  rich and famous in southern california's  orange county  as marissa cooper the rich beautiful and  troubled girl next door barton strikes  up a relationship with brooding outsider  ryan atwood  played by ben mckenzie becomes friends  with seth cohen and summer roberts  played by adam brody and rachel bilson  and deals with school  drinking problems and plenty of ups and  downs with her dramatic and difficult  parents  barton left the show during its third  season after her character was killed in  a car crash  she later admitted that if she could do  it all over again she probably wouldn't  have taken the role though mackenzie  brody and bilson were firmly in their  20s during their time on the oc  barton was just 17 when she started and  in retrospect she said  people say be grateful for what you have  but it was certainly  not the kind of thing i was expecting it  to be  mandy patinkin has been one of the most  recognizable faces in hollywood for  decades but before his long-running role  on showtime's homeland alongside claire  danes  he had a few botched stints on  television  appearing on both chicago hope and  criminal minds for just two seasons  before leaving both shows  as far as chicago hope was concerned  potenkin simply wanted to be able to  spend more time with his family and  couldn't handle the schedule but  criminal minds was a different matter  patinkin signed on to play jason gideon  a criminal profiler with a dark past  but he ended up exiting the series just  two episodes into the third season  due to creative differences which is a  polite way of saying he hated the  material potinkin told new york magazine  that he was shocked by the show's gory  disturbing content  saying i thought it was something very  different i never thought they were  going to kill and rape all these women  every night  every day week after week year after  year  it was very destructive to my soul and  my personality  after that i didn't think i would get to  work in television again  potenkin even went so far as to call the  show his biggest public mistake mincing  no words about his biggest career regret  during the height of game of thrones  which ended its run as one of the most  lauded and watched series of all time  most actors probably would have given  anything for the chance to kill  or be killed in westeros in fact plenty  of performers wound up with stints on  the show which was famous for brutally  murdering its characters  in unexpected ways however it seems as  if at least one actor who spent five  seasons in the seven kingdoms would  rather have not visited the realm  at all stephen delane played stannis  baratheon  brother of the late king robert and  seemingly rightful heir to the throne  however after trying to fight every  obstacle in his path he falls in battle  at the hands of brienne of tarth  played by gwendolyn christie after going  so far as to burn  his own young daughter at the stake as a  war sacrifice  ultimately it turns out delane might  have been just as tortured as the  character he played  he had trouble understanding the  storylines relying on co-star liam  cunningham who played davos  seaworth to explain them even after his  time on thrones delane claimed he would  turn on the show  only to turn it back off again because  he was unable to follow it proving this  notoriously complex series was even  mysterious to some of the actors  involved  when nbc's new sitcom community  premiered in 2009 the cast was a  promising bunch from future atlanta star  donald glover to the hangovers ken  jung to allison brie who would go on to  appear in mad men and glow  plus there was a former saturday night  live star chevy chase who was best known  for his series of national lampoon films  chase infamously parted ways with snl on  negative terms  so it may have been a calculated risk to  give him a role in something as small  as community and in the end it might not  have been the right call  chase stuck it out on community for four  seasons despite several high-profile  tiffs with the show's creator dan harmon  but he never missed the opportunity to  criticize the show in public  telling the huffington post that signing  onto the series was a big mistake  and that as a sitcom the entire project  was the quote  lowest form of television it's no wonder  chevy quit in the middle of the fourth  season by walking off the set  before adult animated series like bojack  horseman  archer and big mouth started to push the  envelope on dirty boundary-breaking  animation there was south park the  original controversial cartoon  no topic was untouchable for creators  matt stone and trey parker  who brought the insane raunchy colorado  town of south park to life with absurd  voice acting heightened situations and  topical references  however one longtime performer on the  show eventually hit his limit  quitting suddenly over a joke that he  thought went way too far  a 2005 episode of south park that  relentlessly skewered scientology  apparently angered isaac hayes a public  scientologist who played chef on the  show  i'm not the reincarnation of l ron  hubbard and  scientology is just a big fat global  scam  at first hayes didn't seem too upset  saying it was all in good fun  but his attitude changed because in  early 2006 hayes issued a statement  saying the show had finally gone too far  citing quote religious intolerance hayes  was released from his contract  but after his passing in 2008 his son  isaac hayes iii  said his father actually suffered a  stroke before that statement was issued  and someone involved with the church of  scientology quit  on his behalf providing a much more  tragic twist to this story than anyone  could have anticipated  the brady bunch trafficked in feel-good  humor and easy goofy jokes  an ensemble cast by nature everyone is  familiar with the story of a man named  brady his wife carol and their sons and  daughters all adjusting to life in a  much bigger family  it was sweet and sappy but according to  the guy who played mike brady the show  could have been  a lot more clever in its execution  robert reed was a classically trained  actor who even attended london's famous  royal academy of dramatic art  the man spent most of his early career  as a shakespearean actor so it's not  surprising that he was unhappy with the  brady bunches material  reed frequently clashed with the show's  producer sherwood schwartz a veteran of  the much sillier gilligan's island and  he would give schwartz unsolicited notes  before flat out refusing to appear in  the show's final episode  as the story goes schwartz wanted to  give reed the axe if the show continued  alas it didn't the brady bunch was  canceled after five  seasons child stars often work to shed  their squeaky clean images as they move  towards adulthood but  few performers have worked harder at  this than miley cyrus  after making her name on disney  channel's hannah montana where she  played a teen girl who's secretly a pop  star cyrus pivoted hard in the post  hannah years making a name for herself  as a controversial and unpredictable  artist  despite her often ridiculous antics  cyrus's undeniable talent has kept her  in the cultural lexicon  and she has said the role definitely  caused some mental challenges but  perhaps that made her who she is today  though miley cyrus says she doesn't  completely regret the show her father  billy ray cyrus who appeared on the show  as miley's father has a totally  different take  in 2011 the achy breaky heart singer  told gq that the show destroyed his  family and that he wished the series had  never happened saying quote  i take it back in a second and that  makes sense considering that he just  split up with his wife and wasn't  speaking to miley at the time  in recent years however it appears that  father and daughter have patched things  up  i just don't want you to die alone dad  the jonas brothers made up of kevin joe  and nick became superstars thanks in  part to the disney channel and original  movies like camp rock  but the brothers have some serious  regrets about their disney channel  series  starting in the spring of 2009 the three  starred in their own show  jonas renamed jonas la in its second and  final season  presenting a fictionalized version of  their lives as a boy band  when jonas la didn't continue past its  second season  it was clearly a huge relief for all  three jonases  in 2013 joe told vulture it just ended  up being some weird slapstick humor that  only a 10 year old would laugh at  we went along with it at the time  because we thought disney was our only  real shot  and we were terrified that it could all  be taken away from us at any moment  apparently all three brothers agreed in  2019 in their amazon documentary chasing  happiness they again admitted they  regretted jonas l.a with nick saying the  show was quote just a bad move  and kevin revealing that the series  definitely wasn't quote  on brand this show was not good  it didn't feel like it was us anymore  the jonas brothers have survived and  thrived in the years since but clearly  they don't spend much time  re-watching episodes of jonas l.a  lost remains one of the biggest  television hits but one of its stars had  a less than positive experience  evangeline lilly who starred as kate  austin for the show's entire run  revealed in a july 2018 episode of the  lost boys podcast that not only was she  unhappy with kate's character arc  but that she was often miserable on set  here's lily on the lost boys talking  about her character  in the beginning she was kind of cool  and then as the show went on i felt like  she became more and more  predictable and obnoxious to make  matters worse lily even detailed some  instances of sexual harassment and  coercion on set when it came to scenes  that required various states of undress  she said in season 3 i'd had a bad  experience on set with being basically  cornered into doing a scene partially  naked  and i felt i had no choice in the matter  i was mortified and i was trembling  and when it finished i was crying my  eyes out however when confronted with a  similar situation in season 4 she  bravely spoke up  i then said that's it no more you can  write whatever you want  but i won't do it i will never take my  clothes off on this show again  and she didn't lily is an mcu superhero  now  but for one dark moment lost left her  feeling powerless  check out one of our newest videos right  here plus even more looper videos about  your favorite stuff are coming soon  subscribe to our youtube channel and hit  the bell so you don't miss a single one

